Selvala taps for mana equal to the greatest power among your creatures, so one big body turns her into a mana engine. The deck ramps with elves into a single huge creature, untaps Selvala to double the mana, and spends it on more huge creatures, each of which also draws a card off her. It ends with Craterhoof Behemoth or a team-wide pump the turn after everything lands.

# The commander
Selvala, Heart of the Wilds :: three mana. {G}, {T}: add X mana in any combination of colours, where X is the greatest power among creatures you control. Whenever another creature enters, its controller may draw a card if its power is greater than every other creature's.
The draw is symmetric. Your 9/9 entering draws you a card; an opponent's creature that becomes the biggest on the battlefield draws THEM one. Keep the biggest creature on your side.
With only Selvala out, X is 2: she needs a fatty or a pump to do anything big.

# Big-mana lines
Selvala, Heart of the Wilds + Bygone Colossus :: warp the Colossus for {3} and Selvala taps for 9 that turn. You draw a card as it enters as the biggest creature. Warp exiles it at end of turn, but you can cast it again later.
Selvala, Heart of the Wilds + Quirion Ranger :: return a Forest to untap Selvala once a turn: the same big X twice.
Selvala, Heart of the Wilds + Scryb Ranger :: the same untap, with flash and protection from blue.
Selvala, Heart of the Wilds + Wirewood Symbiote :: return an Elf (Selvala is one) to untap a creature. Bounce a mana elf to untap Selvala, then replay the elf.
Selvala, Heart of the Wilds + Zopandrel, Hunger Dominus :: Zopandrel doubles every creature's power at the beginning of each combat. Tap Selvala after combat starts and X doubles.
Hyrax Tower Scout :: enters and untaps Selvala.
Temur Sabertooth + Hyrax Tower Scout + Selvala, Heart of the Wilds :: pay {1}{G} to return the Scout and recast it for {2}{G} to untap Selvala; with her own {G}, a loop costs six. Once she taps for seven or more (one 7-power creature), every loop makes mana, as much as you like. Each recast is also a creature entering, which can draw off Selvala. A three-card loop, so it fits Bracket 3.
Great Oak Guardian :: flash; your whole team gets +2/+2 and untaps. X goes up by 2 and Selvala taps again.
Legolas's Quick Reflexes :: split second: untap Selvala with hexproof.
Concordant Crossroads :: everything has haste, so this turn's fatty can attack and Selvala can tap the turn she arrives. Opponents' creatures get haste too.

# Finishers
Craterhoof Behemoth :: haste, and every creature gets trample and +X/+X, where X is the number of creatures you control. With eight creatures out that is usually lethal.
Pathbreaker Ibex :: when it attacks, the team gets trample and +X/+X equal to your greatest power.
Zopandrel, Hunger Dominus :: doubles every creature's power and toughness at each combat.
Finale of Devastation :: with X of ten or more, fetch any creature and give the team +X/+X and haste.
Ghalta, Primal Hunger :: costs {X} less for your creatures' total power: often two mana. A 12/12 trampler and a Selvala draw.
Kogla, the Titan Ape :: fights a creature on entering, and destroys an artifact or enchantment on each attack.
Elder Gargaroth :: a 6/6 that makes a Beast, gains 3 or draws whenever it attacks or blocks.
Garruk, Primal Hunter :: 3/3 Beasts every turn, or −3 to draw equal to your greatest power.
Invasion of Ikoria :: X sets the mana value it fetches from library or graveyard; defeat it in combat for Zilortha.

# Drawing cards
Beast Whisperer :: a card for every creature spell you cast.
Guardian Project :: a card for every new creature with a fresh name.
Regal Force :: a card for each green creature you control.
Rishkar's Expertise :: draw equal to your greatest power, then cast a five-drop free.
Return of the Wildspeaker :: draw equal to your greatest non-Human power, or +3/+3 to the team.
Momentous Fall :: sacrifice a creature: draw cards equal to its power.
Disciple of Freyalise :: sacrifice another creature on entering: draw and gain life equal to its power. It doubles as a land.
Last March of the Ents :: draw equal to your greatest toughness, then put any number of creatures from your hand onto the battlefield.
Sylvan Library :: pick the best of three every turn.
The One Ring :: protection for a turn, then a card every upkeep. Collector Ouphe turns it off.

# Tutor lines — what to fetch, and when
Natural Order -> Craterhoof Behemoth :: sacrifice a green creature (a spent mana elf) and Hoof goes straight onto the battlefield with haste. With five or more other creatures out, swing for the game.
Eldritch Evolution -> Craterhoof Behemoth :: sacrifice a six-drop (Kogla, Pathbreaker Ibex or Disciple of Freyalise) for a creature of mana value up to eight, straight onto the battlefield.
Summoner's Pact -> Craterhoof Behemoth :: free now; pay {2}{G}{G} next upkeep or lose. Only when Selvala can cast the Hoof THIS turn.
Fierce Empath -> Zopandrel, Hunger Dominus :: any creature of mana value 6 or more to hand.
Survival of the Fittest -> Bygone Colossus :: discard any creature to fetch any creature. Discarded fatties come back with Finale of Devastation.
Woodland Bellower -> Priest of Titania :: any nonlegendary green creature of mana value 3 or less, straight onto the battlefield: Priest for mana, Quirion Ranger or Hyrax Tower Scout for untaps.
Green Sun's Zenith -> Quirion Ranger :: X = 1 for the untap engine, or a bigger X for a fatty.
Chord of Calling -> Great Oak Guardian :: instant speed, convoked by your elves.
Nature's Rhythm -> Beast Whisperer :: any creature onto the battlefield; harmonize lets you cast it again from the graveyard.
Shared Summons -> Craterhoof Behemoth :: two creatures with different names to hand: Hoof plus an untap creature.
Tooth and Nail :: entwined at nine mana, it puts Craterhoof and a second fatty straight onto the battlefield.
Turntimber Symbiosis :: puts a creature from your top seven onto the battlefield.
Growing Rites of Itlimoc :: digs four for a creature; with four creatures out at your end step it flips into a land that taps for {G} per creature.
Formidable Speaker :: discard a card to tutor a creature to hand, and it untaps a permanent each turn.

# Mana
Llanowar Elves :: {G} on turn one.
Elvish Mystic :: the second copy.
Fyndhorn Elves :: the third.
Birds of Paradise :: any colour, flying.
Delighted Halfling :: mana that makes Selvala uncounterable.
Arbor Elf :: untaps a Forest; with Utopia Sprawl or Wild Growth, that is two mana.
Priest of Titania :: {G} for every Elf on the battlefield, Selvala included.
Fanatic of Rhonas :: {G}{G}{G}{G} once you have a 4-power creature.
Shang-Chi, Master of Kung Fu :: two mana for creature abilities, and it lets your creatures use tap abilities the turn they arrive.
Elvish Spirit Guide :: a free {G} from your hand.
Utopia Sprawl :: an extra mana from a Forest.
Wild Growth :: the same.
Carpet of Flowers :: free mana each main phase, equal to an opponent's Islands.
Sol Ring :: the usual.
Lotus Petal :: free.
Castle Garenbrig :: six mana for creature spells and abilities.
Nykthos, Shrine to Nyx :: green mana equal to your devotion.
Wirewood Lodge :: untaps an Elf, Selvala included.
Yavimaya, Cradle of Growth :: every land is a Forest, for Arbor Elf and the Rangers.
Gemstone Caverns :: a free extra land when you're not first.
Talon Gates of Madara :: phases a creature out in response to removal.
Dryad Arbor :: a land that is also a green creature for Natural Order.
Slumbering Trudge :: a big body for little mana; it enters stunned.
Sheltering Ancient :: a 5/5 for two. Its upkeep gives counters to an opponent's creature, so it's a short-term Selvala battery.

# Protection and answers
Allosaurus Shepherd :: your green spells can't be countered.
Cavern of Souls :: name your key creature type and it can't be countered.
Autumn's Veil :: blanks blue and black counters and removal for a turn.
Veil of Summer :: the same, and draws a card.
Vines of Vastwood :: hexproof from their spells, or kicked for +4/+4.
Temur Sabertooth :: return a creature to hand to save it (and re-trigger Selvala), and Sabertooth goes indestructible.
Endurance :: flash, free, and shuffles a graveyard away.
Beast Within :: destroys any permanent.
Force of Vigor :: free on their turn: destroy two artifacts or enchantments.
Bridgeworks Battle :: a fight, or a land.
Boseiju, Who Endures :: a land that destroys an artifact, enchantment or nonbasic land.
Collector Ouphe :: shuts off every artifact's activated abilities, your Sol Ring, Lotus Petal and One Ring included. Play it when theirs matter more.
Homeward Path :: gets back creatures they stole.
Emergence Zone :: everything has flash for a turn.
Shifting Woodland :: with delirium, copies a permanent card in your graveyard.

# What to keep in an opening hand
Keep two lands, a mana elf or two, and Selvala. Turn two Selvala off a turn-one elf is the strongest start.
Turn three or four, land one fatty (Bygone Colossus, Ghalta, a tutored six-drop) and Selvala's X jumps to five or more.
Then find an untap creature, double the mana, and find Craterhoof Behemoth with Natural Order or Eldritch Evolution.
